    "q-117181": {
      "dom_id": "step-q117181",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/c3f298b4df4e0c8ff66ad9da970c16ab11839f014519fd451dfba050500d9513.png)\n\nA family is having a picnic in a park. They place a big square blanket on the ground. The dimensions of the blanket are shown in the figure above. What is the area covered by the blanket?",
      "worked_solution": "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\nA={a}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that $a=7\\,ft.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={7}^{2}=49\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
