    "q-53269": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53269",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/91a554b467201b7507b531dcc0b6e1d5d9970d3e6d6554878644a31e5e38d9fa.png)\n\nThe area of the rectangular field shown above is $500\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}.$ What is the value of $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=20\\,yd,\\,A=500\\,{yd}^{2},\\,b=x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b \\\\ 500 & =20\\cdot x \\\\ x & =\\frac{500}{20} \\\\ x & =25\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
