    "q-53279": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53279",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/547debca3e0215ebad8db2c525f9d1b0d435379c081073013cdbfd52b1b6c0f9.png)\n\nThe area of the rectangular court shown above is $56\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}.$ What is the value of $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "The area of a rectangle is given by \n\n$$\nA=a\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFrom the figure, we obtain that \n\n$$\na=2x-6\\,yd,\\,A=56\\,{yd}^{2},\\,b=7\\,\\text{yd}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =a\\cdot b \\\\ 56 & =(2x-6)\\cdot 7 \\\\ 56 & =14x-42 \\\\ 98 & =14x \\\\ x & =7\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
